// Dalvik Bytecode - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// Dalvik bytecode: the magic `dex\n035\0`, a checksum, a 20-byte
// SHA-1 signature, and then a row of lengths that all have to
// agree with each other and with the file.
//
// header_size is 112 and endian_tag is the constant 0x12345678 --
// it is not an endianness, it is a byte-order mark, and a reader
// that got it backwards would know. file_size is the field that
// catches a truncated dump, which is the failure this file is most
// likely to have.
//
// Hello World! follows the header.
//
// dex: 116 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 64 65 78 0A 30 33 35 00 EF BE AD DE 00 01 02 03 |dex.035.........|   <- 0000
// 04 05 06 07 08 09 0A 0B 0C 0D 0E 0F 10 11 12 13 |................|   <- 0010
// 74 00 00 00 70 00 00 00 78 56 34 12 00 00 00 00 |t...p...xV4.....|   <- 0020
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 0C 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0030
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0040
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0050
// 00 00 00 00 70 00 00 00 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F |....p...Hello Wo|   <- 0060
// 72 6C 64 21                                     |rld!|   <- 0070
